1
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:20,000
What is CertaRig?
Presented by Chintan Dedhia

2
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Work does not end when the sensors are wired.
It begins there.

3
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Procedures, screenshots, and a story
that is hard to audit.

4
00:00:48,000 --> 00:01:05,000
People speak English.
Rigs speak numbers.

5
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:18,000
4.2 bar is not a vibe.
15 L/min is not “about that high.”

6
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Who is allowed to energize the output?

7
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:55,000
The agent interprets.
The kernel decides.

8
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:20,000
The agent can ask.
Only the kernel can say yes.

9
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:50,000
End customer: the person who owns the bench.
Not a chatbot user.

10
00:02:50,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Mapped rigs.
Not unknown machines.

11
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:50,000
MQTT · Modbus · OPC UA
S7 · EtherNet/IP · CAN

12
00:03:50,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Same kernel. Different rig.json.
Observe first.

13
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Build-time AI: Grok 4.6
It never drives the relay.

14
00:04:45,000 --> 00:05:15,000
Runtime default: Fake
Proven on CI and the 12 Sep bench.

15
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Live fallbacks: Claude Sonnet 4.5
then OpenAI / OpenAI-compatible.

16
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:40,000
Benchmark: skill routing and tool discipline.
Not chat quality.

17
00:05:40,000 --> 00:06:10,000
Six gates.
Observe before actuation.

18
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:25,000
Twin, then arm, then restore.

19
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:45,000
Pressure peak 4.83 bar against 4.2
Flow peak 15.41 L/min against 15.0

20
00:06:45,000 --> 00:07:00,000
OUTPUT = enabled AND permit
AND not tripped AND E-stop closed AND healthy

21
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:45,000
Phase 3 dashboard · port 8080
Observe only

22
00:07:45,000 --> 00:08:15,000
Studio · Live
Both channels, trip lines, ready-to-arm

23
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:35,000
A human applies the map.
No invented skill on a live output.

24
00:08:35,000 --> 00:09:10,000
Fake agent selects the skill.
Kernel compares the number.

25
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:45,000
4.2 bar · kernel trip
Output latched safe

26
00:09:45,000 --> 00:10:15,000
15 L/min · independent trip
Same output

27
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:35,000
Shutdown needs a human.
Kernel forces safe first.

28
00:10:35,000 --> 00:11:00,000
Checksummed evidence is the output
of the procedure.

29
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:12,000
Capstone: deploy the agent
on someone else's rig

30
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:28,000
Interview: modules, bus, pins,
trips, observe-only

31
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:40,000
Agent proposes a map.
A human still applies it.

32
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:50,000
Twin, then arm.
The interview is not built yet.

33
00:11:50,000 --> 00:12:05,000
The AI never had to own
the dangerous decision.

34
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:20,000
Phase 3 is complete.
Put this on any mapped bench.

